---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { u } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility"
  description="The University of Mars accessibility statement, including the WCAG 2.1 AA commitment and how to report a barrier."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Access office"
    title="Accessibility"
    lede="The University of Mars works to meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA on its public websites and to provide equitable access to programs."
    crumbs={[{ href: '/accessibility/', label: 'Accessibility' }]}
  >
    <p class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn" href={u('/support/?category=accessibility#request')}>Report a barrier</a>
    </p>
  </PageHero>
  <article class="prose wrap narrow">
    <h2>Commitment</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to conform to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at Level AA. That covers public pages,
      applications used in courses, and documents we publish as the official version of a policy. Where a legacy PDF
      falls short, the office will provide the same information in another format.
    </p>
    <p>
      Academic accommodations are handled one student at a time. The web standard is the floor for the public site, not
      a limit on what an accommodation can include.
    </p>
    <h2 id="display-settings">Display settings</h2>
    <p>
      Every page has a <strong>Display</strong> button in the header. The settings stay in this browser and follow you
      from page to page. Nothing is sent to the university.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Theme:</strong> Light, Dark, or System, which follows your device and changes when it does.</li>
      <li><strong>Text size:</strong> 90% to 140% of your browser’s text size. Pages reflow instead of scrolling sideways.</li>
      <li><strong>Dyslexia-friendly font:</strong> OpenDyslexic, with wider letter, word, and line spacing.</li>
      <li><strong>Reduce motion:</strong> turns off animation and smooth scrolling. It starts from your device setting.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The dark theme is held to the same WCAG 2.1 AA contrast target as the light theme. Photos are dimmed slightly so
      they do not glare against dark backgrounds.
    </p>
    <h2>Report a barrier</h2>
    <p>Tell us the page address, what you were trying to do, and the tool you were using, such as a browser or a screen reader. A phone call is enough if that is easier.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Help Center category: Accessibility, subcategory Barrier on campus</li>
      <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.accessEmail}`}>{site.accessEmail}</a></li>
      <li>Phone: <a href={site.accessHref}>{site.accessPhone}</a>, weekdays 9 a.m. to 4 p.m.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The office acknowledges barrier reports within two business days and says what will change, or what equivalent
      access it can offer while a fix is underway.
    </p>
    <h2>Accommodations</h2>
    <p>
      Students who need an academic or housing accommodation should read
      <a href={u('/support/articles/accommodations/')}>how to request one</a>. Faculty who need a classroom change write
      to the same office.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
